Z||000000||86SE||02-25-2000||08:59 PM||||I found a silver switch under the right hand side of the dash.  If I reach my right hand up underneath the dash and go about 6-8 inches right of the stering colum, there it is!!  I just cant figure out what its used for....and if its from the factory, why is it hidden under the dash??<P>Its an 86 SE V-6 if it helps.....||||reg||5
Z||000001||ounmongk||02-25-2000||11:05 PM||||I wanna say it's the Neutral start switch. I'm not too sure though.. there's only one way to find out what the switch does though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Maybe it's for the ejector seats... don't want your finger to slip on that one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||02-25-2000||11:22 PM||||When I bought my 86GT, it already had a remote starter installed.  There is a little switch mounted just as you describe for disabling the remote for service etc. Could yours be the same?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-26-2000||12:41 AM||||I could also be from a previous alarm system or an ignition cut-off switch. Why not flip it and see if the car starts?||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||02-26-2000||03:14 AM||||OK, i folloed the wires coming off the switch (two wires).  1 went straight up for 3 inches then bolted to the chassis.  The second wire ran all the way down the stering colum to a little black box that said "PARAGRAM Security Systems".  Hmmmmmm, so I checked the fuse, fuse is ok.  Followd 2 more of the 4 wires that came out of the box and they led the the Fuse block, into the Circuit Braker fuses.  <P>I think the fuses are still good, because my power windows still work and my rear window defogger still works. <P>I can turn the switch on or off and the car still starts.  Anybody know how these security systems work??||||reg||5
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||02-26-2000||04:53 AM||||Dunno, but be careful. A lot of lives have ended with the phrase "What does this button do?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000006||Oreif||02-26-2000||11:01 AM||||Since you found the alarm brain box see if it attaches to the large red and large purple wires on the steering column. If it does it may cut-off your ignition. Also I would try and find some info on the alarm since you know it's brand. some alarm systems when activated require another switch to de-activate. If you don't know how then don't turn it on. One last thing I would actually think about removing it. Most alarm systems have a battery drop circuit. If the battery goes below 9volts the alarm automatically triggers on. So if your battery gets weak over time or you disconnect your battery when you hook it back up the car may not start.||||reg||1
